# Client quality

Write code a client reviewer can follow. Clarity beats cleverness.

## Do

- One job per file. Names from the roadmap (`useTrendingMovies`, `signOut`, `MovieCard`).
- Handle loading, empty, and error on every screen that fetches.
- Hide Staff Pick when its query fails. Never take Home down with it.
- Keep functions short enough to explain out loud.

## Do not

- Use `any`, `ts-ignore`, or non-null assertions to silence the compiler
- Leave debug buttons, logs, or sample routes in a finished phase
- Add a library to avoid a few lines of `StyleSheet`
- Invent product behavior that the Flutter app does not have

## When unsure

Choose the option the roadmap already names. If it is silent, choose the smaller change and note it in `docs/project_log.md`.
